    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to demonstrate divergence and rollback",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**For `bad_lr`.** Follow the learning-rate jump, loss and gradient blowup, then the **DIVERGENCE / ROLLBACK** command. The trainer's **response** should report restoring a checkpoint; loss and gradients should recover as training resumes.\n\n**Run = All** compares divergence runs in the selected time range. The control-loop dots show command delivery and response time."
      },
      "id": 1
    },
